  "slug": "cryo-em-47d2",
  "summary": "Contaminants and heterogeneous mixtures degrade cryo-EM particle selection, prompting picking methods coupled to downstream reconstruction.",
  "synthesis": "The dominant thread across these three preprints is handling contaminating and heterogeneous species during cryo-EM particle selection and reconstruction. CryoAnomaly trains an anomaly detector on clean synthetic cryo-EM data and uses it to suppress real contaminants as hard negatives in few-shot picking. A reconstruction-aware pipeline integrates picking, contamination removal, and 2D class selection, linking the picking step to downstream reconstruction. The meta-algorithm addresses complex mixtures at the reconstruction level, spawning and aggregating multi-class ab initio reconstructions and reporting accuracy on Tomotwin-100 subsets and recovery of ribosomal components. The new elements are anomaly-based negative suppression and the explicit coupling of picking with reconstruction rather than treating picking as an isolated preprocessing step. All results are preprint-level and not independently validated.",
  "synthesis_model": "claude-haiku-5-5",
  "synthesized_on": "2026-08-30"
}
